# .gitignore for .NET 8 projects created in Visual Studio 2022
# Keeps build outputs, user-specific files, IDE state and package artifacts out of source control.

## Build artifacts
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
publish/

## Visual Studio
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## Rider / JetBrains
.idea/
*.sln.iml
_ReSharper*/
*.DotSettings.user

## Visual Studio Code
.vscode/

## NuGet / packages
packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/

## Test results
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

## Logs, temporary files
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*.cache

## Sensitive / machine-specific
*.pfx
*.key
*.p12

## Publish / deployment
*.Publish.xml
appsettings.*.json     # ignore environment-specific appsettings if you store secrets locally

# Rider / VS caches
.idea/